            <ArticleTitle>The use of injectable nitroglycerin in the cardiac catheterization laboratory. Nitroglycerin in cardiac catheterization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>319-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>At our institution, injectable nitroglycerin (TNG) has been employed during cardiac catheterization since 1976. Initially, it was primarily used in patients undergoing a provocative test for coronary spasm with ergonovine maleate. After the initial favorable experience, the use of injectable TNG became routine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
